                    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
                    "body": "I'm not sure how to call them, but by \"global keys\" I meant built-in keys. For example, if I only press `d` or `a` to show what other follow-up keys are available. Or to show if I didn't have any keys pressed, what keys are available, because I have a key that is mapped to `J` letter, but I'm not sure how to display the clue for it.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I'm not sure how to call them, but by \"global keys\" I meant built-in keys. For example, if I only press <code class=\"notranslate\">d</code> or <code class=\"notranslate\">a</code> to show what other follow-up keys are available. Or to show if I didn't have any keys pressed, what keys are available, because I have a key that is mapped to <code class=\"notranslate\">J</code> letter, but I'm not sure how to display the clue for it.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "I'm not sure how to call them, but by \"global keys\" I meant built-in keys. For example, if I only press d or a to show what other follow-up keys are available. Or to show if I didn't have any keys pressed, what keys are available, because I have a key that is mapped to J letter, but I'm not sure how to display the clue for it.",
