                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "I see.\r\n\r\nThis is not supported right away from the box by 'mini.clue'. As I said earlier, it works *only* for and starting with **opt-in** triggers. For example, `<Leader>`, `g`, etc. Here is an [example](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/1cd8d7e8318071eddc536815f5cafe50b012ac29/doc/mini-clue.txt#L243).\r\n\r\nIt also only shows info about mappings automatically or [manually set up clues](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/1cd8d7e8318071eddc536815f5cafe50b012ac29/doc/mini-clue.txt#L325). This matters for your examples:\r\n- `d` usually starts an Operator-pending mode and usually doesn't have mappings starting with it (so clues probably won't get shown);\r\n- `a` inside Visual or Operator-pending mode may not have many mappings defined after it. For example, 'mini.ai' treats `a` as key itself and doesn't create separate mappings for every textobject it implements (for good reasons of allowing easier buffer-local config and not relying on 'timeoutlen' option).\r\n\r\nThis all might have sounded a bit technical, but the bottom line is that 'mini.clue' is not specifically designed for the task you're wondering. To a certain extent it can be achieved, but I'd suggest to not embark on this journey.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I see.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is not supported right away from the box by 'mini.clue'. As I said earlier, it works <em>only</em> for and starting with <strong>opt-in</strong> triggers. For example, <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;Leader&gt;</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">g</code>, etc. Here is an <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/1cd8d7e8318071eddc536815f5cafe50b012ac29/doc/mini-clue.txt#L243\">example</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It also only shows info about mappings automatically or <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/1cd8d7e8318071eddc536815f5cafe50b012ac29/doc/mini-clue.txt#L325\">manually set up clues</a>. This matters for your examples:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">d</code> usually starts an Operator-pending mode and usually doesn't have mappings starting with it (so clues probably won't get shown);</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">a</code> inside Visual or Operator-pending mode may not have many mappings defined after it. For example, 'mini.ai' treats <code class=\"notranslate\">a</code> as key itself and doesn't create separate mappings for every textobject it implements (for good reasons of allowing easier buffer-local config and not relying on 'timeoutlen' option).</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This all might have sounded a bit technical, but the bottom line is that 'mini.clue' is not specifically designed for the task you're wondering. To a certain extent it can be achieved, but I'd suggest to not embark on this journey.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "I see.\nThis is not supported right away from the box by 'mini.clue'. As I said earlier, it works only for and starting with opt-in triggers. For example, <Leader>, g, etc. Here is an example.\nIt also only shows info about mappings automatically or manually set up clues. This matters for your examples:\n\nd usually starts an Operator-pending mode and usually doesn't have mappings starting with it (so clues probably won't get shown);\na inside Visual or Operator-pending mode may not have many mappings defined after it. For example, 'mini.ai' treats a as key itself and doesn't create separate mappings for every textobject it implements (for good reasons of allowing easier buffer-local config and not relying on 'timeoutlen' option).\n\nThis all might have sounded a bit technical, but the bottom line is that 'mini.clue' is not specifically designed for the task you're wondering. To a certain extent it can be achieved, but I'd suggest to not embark on this journey.",
